---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { checkerUrl, sitePath } from '../../lib/urls';
---

<Page
  article
  title="How to read MutualLens snapshot history"
  description="Compare compatible saved relationship reports without confusing save time, source collection time, observed absence, or a verified unfollow."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">GUIDE · SAVED SNAPSHOTS</p><h1>
    A snapshot preserves a report, not a motive.
  </h1><p class="lede">
    Saving two reports can show how their supplied records differ. The result is
    only as comparable as the account identity, collection dates and source
    scope recorded with both snapshots.
  </p>
  <h2>Save time and source time are different</h2><p>
    MutualLens records when you save a snapshot in the browser. That timestamp
    does not say when Instagram collected the relationship files. Historical
    comparison needs known, ordered source collection dates; the date you
    downloaded, opened or imported a file cannot substitute for a missing source
    date.
  </p>
  <h2>Label the account before saving</h2><p>
    Basic upload comparison does not require a username. Snapshot comparison
    does need evidence that both reports describe the same account. Add the same
    optional account label before saving when a stable account ID is not
    available. Username-only matching still carries rename, reactivation and
    username-reuse uncertainty.
  </p>
  <h2>Compare compatible sources</h2><ul>
    <li>
      Choose the genuinely earlier collection as the first snapshot and the
      later, non-overlapping collection as the second.
    </li><li>
      Keep source formats and adapter versions compatible. Uploaded-file and
      automatic-source reports describe different evidence scopes.
    </li><li>
      Uploaded-file comparisons preserve any skipped-row, missing-part or
      ambiguous-identity warnings from both reports.
    </li><li>
      Automatic-source history needs complete, terminal lists in both
      directions. A partial automatic scan cannot establish a confirmed
      negative.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Read the four change groups literally</h2>
  <div class="comparison-table">
    <table>
      <caption
        >What a comparison between two compatible snapshots reports</caption
      >
      <thead
        ><tr><th scope="col">Group</th><th scope="col">Meaning</th></tr></thead
      >
      <tbody>
        <tr
          ><th scope="row">Followers present later</th><td
            >Absent from the earlier supplied followers list; present in the
            later one.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><th scope="row">Followers absent later</th><td
            >Present in the earlier supplied followers list; absent from the
            later one.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><th scope="row">Following present later</th><td
            >Absent from the earlier supplied following list; present in the
            later one.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><th scope="row">Following absent later</th><td
            >Present in the earlier supplied following list; absent from the
            later one.</td
          ></tr
        >
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    “Absent later” is not an exact unfollow timestamp. A platform-side change,
    username change, account state, incomplete source or collection-window
    difference may also explain the observation. The checker does not assign a
    reason or intent.
  </p>
  <h2>Know where local copies live</h2><p>
    Nothing is saved automatically. When you choose to save, the snapshot is
    stored in IndexedDB on the checker’s browser origin. Other people using the
    same browser profile may be able to view it. Browser cleanup, private
    browsing or a different checker address can make it unavailable.
  </p><p>
    Export a snapshot if you need your own backup. “Delete all local snapshots”
    removes the app-controlled copies on that checker origin, but it cannot
    remove files you already downloaded or browser-managed backups.
  </p>
  <div class="article-actions">
    <a class="button primary" href={checkerUrl('history')}
      >Open saved snapshots <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
    ><a href={sitePath('/guides/not-following-back-vs-unfollowed/')}
      >Why a difference is not proof of an unfollow</a
    >
  </div>
</Page>
